pan style=\"color:#f92672\"\u003ename\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan style=\"color:#ae81ff\"\u003eflux-system\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"why-does-this-help\"\u003eWhy does this help?\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe tailscale kubernetes operator automitically uses a secret named \u0026lsquo;operator-oauth\u0026rsquo; with the stringData matching \u0026lsquo;client_id\u0026rsquo; and \u0026lsquo;client_secret\u0026rsquo; \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cem\u003emeaning\u003c/em\u003e \u003cbr\u003e\nas long as the secret is created before the config file is applied, the secret automatically gets pulled into tailscale.\u003c/p\u003e\n","description":null,"image":null,"permalink":"https://that1linuxguy.github.io/Resume/blogs/tailscale/","title":"Tailscale Kubernetes Operator"}]